  <LifeLessons.ProficiencyDef ParentName="ProficiencyBase">
    <defName>Electronics</defName>
    <label>Electronics</label>
    <generationRules>
      <textbookValue>800</textbookValue>
      <neurotrainerValue>3200</neurotrainerValue>
      <bookTradeTags>
        <li>LLTextbooksUncommon</li>
      </bookTradeTags>
      <neurotrainerTradeTags>
        <li>LLNeurotrainerUncommon</li>
      </neurotrainerTradeTags>
    </generationRules>
    <proficiencyAdjective>electronic</proficiencyAdjective>
    <category>ProficiencyCategory_FabricationAdvanced</category>
    <description>Understanding of electrical properties, electronic circuits and tools. The ability to prepare electrical diagrams and troubleshoot systems.</description>
    <costPractical>2000</costPractical>
    <costTheoretical>2000</costTheoretical>
    <canBePioneered>true</canBePioneered>
    <effectiveSubjectLimit>2</effectiveSubjectLimit>
    <learningEffectivenessLossPerSubject>0.2</learningEffectivenessLossPerSubject>
    <viewerX>6</viewerX>
    <viewerY>4.5</viewerY>
    <prerequisites>
      <li>AdvancedFabrication</li>
      <li>AdvancedScience</li>
    </prerequisites>
    <color>RGBA(0.941, 0.902, 0.549, 1.000)</color>
    <thoughtIcons>
      <li>UI/Buttons/UsePlanetDayNightSystem</li>
      <li>Things/Mote/Disoriented</li>
    </thoughtIcons>
    <theoreticalLearningActivityDefs>
      <li>
        <def>LLDraft</def>
      </li>
      <li>
        <def>LLDocument</def>
      </li>
      <li>
        <def>LLBrainstorm</def>
      </li>
    </theoreticalLearningActivityDefs>
    <practicalLearningActivityDefs>
      <li>
        <def>LLTinkerWithComponents</def>
      </li>
      <li>
        <def>LLAnalyzeGadget</def>
      </li>
      <li>
        <def>LLAnalyzeConstruction</def>
      </li>
    </practicalLearningActivityDefs>
    <assignmentTips>Catch all for almost all industrial buildings and recipes. Represents both the instllation and creation of electronic circuits and components. Used to lockout any workbench or recipe that involves electricity, as well as their associated research projects. May be used with Medical for very-low-tier bionics. May be used with AdvancedFabrication for laser based recipes. Very accomplished medival inventors might have discovered this. Most industrial inventors, mechanics, fabricators, and engineers will have this.</assignmentTips>
  </LifeLessons.ProficiencyDef>
  <LifeLessons.ProficiencyDef ParentName="ProficiencyBase">
    <defName>Construction</defName>
    <label>Construction</label>
    <generationRules>
      <textbookValue>300</textbookValue>
      <neurotrainerValue>1000</neurotrainerValue>
    </generationRules>
    <category>ProficiencyCategory_Construction</category>
    <description>Understanding of basic construction techniques for general purpose furniture or structures.</description>
    <costPractical>600</costPractical>
    <viewerX>5</viewerX>
    <viewerY>9</viewerY>
    <prerequisites>
      <li>BasicMathematics</li>
    </prerequisites>
    <color>RGBA(0.392, 0.584, 0.929, 1.000)</color>
    <thoughtIcons>
      <li>UI/Buttons/UsePlanetDayNightSystem</li>
      <li>Things/Mote/Disoriented</li>
    </thoughtIcons>
    <assignmentTips>Generally used for all-purpose carpentry or masonry. Any construction, mason, or carpenter backstory can have this. Generally does not include anything with electronics. Can be used with BasicFabrication for buildings with adornments or tools - such as tool cabinets. Can be used with Electronics for early electrical constructions like saws. Generally not used for research lockouts.</assignmentTips>
  </LifeLessons.ProficiencyDef>
  <LifeLessons.ProficiencyDef ParentName="ProficiencyBase">
