      <li>Electronics</li>
      <li>Construction</li>
      <li>Physics</li>
      <li>Mechanics</li>
    </prerequisites>
    <color>RGBA(0.733, 0.733, 0.733, 1.000)</color>
    <thoughtIcons>
      <li>UI/Buttons/UsePlanetDayNightSystem</li>
      <li>Things/Mote/Disoriented</li>
    </thoughtIcons>
    <theoreticalLearningActivityDefs>
      <li>
        <def>LLDocument</def>
      </li>
      <li>
        <def>LLBrainstorm</def>
      </li>
      <li>
        <def>LLDraft</def>
      </li>
    </theoreticalLearningActivityDefs>
    <practicalLearningActivityDefs>
      <li>
        <def>LLTinkerWithAdvancedComponents</def>
      </li>
      <li>
        <def>LLAnalyzeConstruction</def>
      </li>
      <li>
        <def>LLAnalyzeGadget</def>
      </li>
      <li>
        <def>LLReverseEngineerGadget</def>
      </li>
    </practicalLearningActivityDefs>
    <assignmentTips>Mastery of mechanical and electrical systems. Ability to both build and design complex systems of machines. Does not include a mastery of space-worthy vessels. Most backstories that use the word "engineer" include this. Unheard of pre-industrial. Knowledge is not sufficient for mastery - represents years of experience as well, so even genius inventory child backstories will not include this. Used to lockout robotics, complex vehicles, simple ship parts, mechs, and factories. Used to lockout advanced weapons recipes. Used to lockout associated research projects.</assignmentTips>
  </LifeLessons.ProficiencyDef>
